      "invariant_id": "N_SOURCE",
      "role": "source",
      "file": "libass/ass.c",
      "function": "process_event_tail",
      "line": 353,
      "operands": [
        "event->Text"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "same_object",
        "left": "event->Text",
        "right": "event->Text",
        "description": "Source identity relation for the vulnerability-relevant value."
      },
      "verified": true,
      "fine_trace_step": 1,
      "description": "Source. `process_event_tail()` first materializes the attacker-controlled `Text` field as heap string `event->Text`. For the witness this duplicates the exact event text `{\\fn@}`, creating the 7-byte allocation that later holds the `\\fn` argument and is over-read at the sink."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "r_hash_input_len_must_be_positive",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "libass/ass_utils.h",
      "function": "fnv_32a_buf",
      "line": 191,
      "operands": [
        "0",
        "len"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": "0",
        "right": "len"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_hash_input_len_must_be_positive",
      "fine_trace_step": 5,
      "description": "Root cause. `fnv_32a_buf()` reaches this `switch` even when `len == 0`. Because the vulnerable source has no early `if (!len) return hval;` guard, `len % 4 == 0` selects `case 0` and the `do { ... } while (--n > 0)` body executes once despite `n` having been computed as 0."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_case2_sink_reached_with_advanced_bp",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "libass/ass_utils.h",
      "function": "fnv_32a_buf",
      "line": 194,
      "operands": [
        "buf",
        "bp"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": "buf",
        "right": "bp"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_case2_sink_reached_with_advanced_bp",
      "fine_trace_step": 6,
      "description": "ASan crash site. After `fnv_32a_buf()` has already consumed the `}` byte and the terminating NUL from the 7-byte `event->Text` allocation, the next fallthrough `*bp++` at line 194 reaches the first heap-redzone byte just past that allocation."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_vertical_prefix_strip_produces_empty_family",
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_vertical_prefix_strip_produces_empty_family",
      "role": "intermediate",
      "file": "libass/ass_parse.c",
      "function": "update_font",
      "line": 111,
      "fine_trace_step": 3,
      "state": "When `update_font()` strips the leading vertical-font marker `@`, it leaves `desc.family.len == 0`; that empty family string is the source-level value later passed into `fnv_32a_buf()`.",
      "operands": [
        "0",
        "desc.family.len"
      ],
